'' A SPAWN ARGUMENT IS CONVERTED THE WAY A CALL ARGUMENT IS. The parser desugars
'' 'spawn f( a )' into '(*frame).__ARG_0 = a', and the field has f's PARAMETER type. For
'' an argument of another UDT that assignment was a BITWISE copy: 'spawn Produce( ch )'
'' over 'byval c as SendChan( of long )' put the Channel's pointer in the frame without
'' a reference, the frame's delete released one nobody held, and the caller's next
'' Receive read freed memory -- exit 139 where fbc prints 'done'. On an ordinary type the
'' same assignment was TKO0738 instead, and 'spawn Use( src )' did not compile at all.
''
'' Now the value is built through the converting constructor into a temporary, assigned
'' into the frame with the type's own let, and the temporary destroyed: argument passing,
'' which fbc does in its invoke. Pinned: the constructor, the let, no decline, no error.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -mt --dump-ir -i toolchains/tiko-windows/inc tests/mir/src/spawn-conv-arg.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' A BY-VALUE AGGREGATE (a std module's, or the test's own): macos-arm64 refuses it until AAPCS64 lands.
'' EXPECT-EXIT[macos-arm64]: 1
'' EXPECT-OUT[macos-arm64]: error TKO0992: not implemented in this build: an aggregate passed or returned by value on macos-arm64
'' EXPECT-OUT: call void _ZN4VIEWC1ER7COUNTED(
'' EXPECT-OUT: call void _ZN4VIEWaSERKS_(
'' EXPECT-OUT: call void _ZN3STD5TASKS8SendChanIiEC1ER7ChannelIiE(
'' EXPECT-OUT: call void _ZN8SendChanIiEaSERKS0_(
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' EXPECT-NOT: TKO0738
